  "scope": "Typed C++/Python histogram workflow authoring, closed V5 portable intent and inline bin/range/log controls in both shared ImGui launchers, preserving original captures and V4 compatibility.",
  "semantics": "NativeWorkflowHistogramOptions holds TargetHistogramOptions and log_counts; optional authored_options is independent of original. A capture or explicit choices is required; original is optional for new authored intent. Every supplied original validates fully even when overridden/disabled. Workflow admission and execution share the existing command option validator and resolve authored commands against each preceding detached stage. No new defaults or pixel/sample/calibration domains are admitted.",
  "transport": "V5 is emitted only for authored histogram choices. Every histogram in V5 has options null (retain original) or exactly binning/bins/range/log_counts. Other V5 kinds retain V4 fields. V1/V2/V3/V4 retain their previous encodings when authored choices are absent. Mixed retained/authored programs, native session batch common/override programs and setup records carry V5. Restoring all original choices canonicalizes back to V4. A missing capture does not synthesize historical evidence.",
  "ui": "Each histogram offers Use edited histogram choices, explicit-range/bin controls or the raw 256-bin profile, and Log counts. Original choices can be restored; capture-free authored steps keep explicit choices. Numeric changes invalidate confirmation/results without changing plane/ROI binding. Kept programs reopen with authored choices; running the retained table does not duplicate its record. Standalone defaults and original command records remain unchanged. Invalid choices refuse preparation with no image/history/Results/file effects.",
  "verification": "555 selected Python checks per OS including 41 new native API checks and ten new input checks; five native executable suites per OS and fresh installed SDK consumers. Independent readers verify 64 reports / 21715 raw input frames, including 20 new option reports / 2096 frames. New input cases keep/reopen custom bins/range/log, raw processor choices, original restoration, invalid choices and capture-free authorship. Tests cover closed V5 grammar, exact integer/Boolean/range admission, immutable values/history, UInt8/UInt16/Float32 and 1/5/65536 bins, ordered stages, disabled validation, batch/setup transport and unchanged V4 behavior. No complete ImageJ/Fiji source/reference/resource/real-GPU/OS-desktop/platform acceptance.",
  "memory": "Authored options have fixed-size value storage, charged in retained program admission; command/target/kernel and cumulative workflow budgets remain unchanged in kind. Frontend argument/getter/draft/diagnostic copies, source/provider caches, allocator overhead and total process RSS remain external.",
